{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1531480-a-simpler-mage-the-awakening","id":1531480,"title":"A \"Simpler\" Mage the Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-25T11:00:52-08:00","id":1531480,"title":"A \"Simpler\" Mage the Awakening","content":"Hi! Like the title says, I'm looking for any ideas, suggestions, hacks or rules implementation that could help me streamline the game experience in Mage, specially regarding spellcasting.<br /> <br /> As a bit of background, I've run several campaigns of Mage the Awakening through both editions of the game, and I love the setting to death. However, I've acquired a significant system fatigue and I'm looking for ways to hack the game in ways that allow me a quicker adjudication of game rules during play. I really like the detailed and intricate system for 2nd edition storytelling system, but in practice it's just to much to keep track off. Add in the heavily structured spellcasting system and the end result is that I end up feeling frustrated and my pacing ruined.<br /> <br /> Please, I'm looking for new ideas, not just the usual 'go back to play 1st ed', or 'you just need to memorize better'. I've tried all of those things already, and especially for my players they haven't really worked out. My players get easily confused with too much calculations and they prefer the play experience to flow with as little game rules as possible.<br /> <br /> I've considered even hacking VtM5 or using Storypath Ultra for our Mage chronicle, but I'd prefer not to jump to a completely different system, if possible.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T11:09:08-08:00","id":1531481,"title":"","content":"To make mechanical suggestions I would need to know what specific points are causing hangups.<br /> <br /> Before that, the only advice I can provide is &quot;make default profiles of spells that are used often and have reference sheets for the Scale and Duration charts.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T05:45:01-08:00","id":1531677,"title":"","content":"First thing I would suggest is a physical cheat board for spellcasting.<br /> <br /> That is a piece of cardboard with counters on it to move around representing the reach, spell factors, range etc. (I don't know how to present this, but it should have a slider for reach in one colour and spell factors in another... Along with tracking paradox in a third colour).<br /> <br /> That along with simplifying yantras, only going into details on what they are using for +3 yantras and higher, for +2 only use the normal limitations (like high speech not being usable reflexively) and just let them take as many +1s as they want (unless it is for flavouring the scene).<br /> <br /> Aside, here is my ranges table:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> +0 Reach: self/touch/touching in combat (dex + brawl/weaponry)/thrown spell( Gnosis + higher of athletics/firearms - subject's defence\u2020)<br /> +1 Reach: sensory/sympathetic range\u2021<br /> +2 Reach: remote viewing (must be live) <br /> <br /> \u2020subject does not get defence if you have the fast spells merit<br /> \u2021sympathetic range is an attainment, which requires Space 2, and 1 mana, and a sympathic yantra, and a sympathy connection - which is used to withstand the spell (weaker the connection the higher the withstand). </div> </div> </div>Now, if you can physically make something and it is still too complicated, you can physically see what can be taken out.<br /> <br /> Lastly, the down&amp;dirty spell casting rules exist for a reason, and do not roll for any spells when the outcome isn't important. In downtime/low stakes situations, just let every spell get one success automatically - to push the narrative forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T06:27:34-08:00","id":1531680,"title":"","content":"I think a cheat sheet would be of great help, I saw <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gQrM0rX7MEyyBgWWDIcHR4Rb15bxJqV5GP7RQXhIeQo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">this one </a>and it looked pretty well made. You can keep track of a lot of things with tokens. The only needed clarification is that taking a penalty in step 3 moves one factor of your choice to a new tier, rather than all of them. It abstracts away things like penalties above -10 and Paradox calculations, but as far as getting the basics down, it seems like a solid resource.<br /> <br /> I think printing individual ones with tokens for players, plus leaving the core book open in the effect quick reference pages (123-127), would make life much easier for you players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T06:33:31-08:00","id":1531681,"title":"","content":"I don't like the &quot;determine your reach&quot; calculation, it is poorly phrased.<br /> <br /> Mainly the +1 at the end, like noo. Let me think. You get 1 reach for having the dots to cast a spell, and 1 extra for each dot exceeding the required dots.<br /> <br /> That's not much better is it?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, remove the +1, but stick it I to Instant cast. So Ritual cast cost -1 reach.<br /> <br /> Tbh, I love the reach system, it is so much better than the hard limit in 1e of &quot;you need an extra dot in the arcanum to make the spell extra...&quot; So indefinite Making spells were impossible before Archmastery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}